<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  node_exporter for the company MacBook Air.

  Deliberately NOT `brew services start node_exporter`, which is what the Mac
  Mini uses: brew’s own plist takes no arguments, and this one needs the
  collector.textfile.directory flag so ps-sampler’s .prom output is picked up.

  The copy on that host said "Installed by install.sh" and was in no repo. It had
  drifted out of version control, or was never in it, and the sentence claiming
  otherwise is why nobody looked. Committed 2026-09-04.

  no-collector.thermal is the point of that commit. macOS exposes no CPU power or
  thermal reading that node_exporter’s darwin collector can take, so it returned
  node_scrape_collector_success{collector="thermal"} 0 on every scrape, forever:
  the only failing collector of thirteen on that host, and a red that can never
  go green teaches a reader to stop looking at reds.

  Turning it off is only half. A collector that is simply absent makes "this host
  cannot measure temperature" indistinguishable from "temperature is fine", and
  the second is the more dangerous reading. install.sh writes
  node_thermal_supported 0 into the textfile directory beside this, so the
  absence is a series carrying a reason rather than a silence.

  No double hyphen anywhere in this comment: it is illegal inside an XML comment,
  plutil accepts it and plistlib does not, and the copy this replaces had one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.homelab.dev-node-exporter</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/node_exporter</string>
        <string>--web.listen-address=127.0.0.1:9100</string>
        <string>--collector.textfile.directory=/Users/rainforest/.local/state/dev-telemetry/textfile</string>
        <string>--no-collector.thermal</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/rainforest/Library/Logs/dev-node-exporter.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/rainforest/Library/Logs/dev-node-exporter.log</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>
    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>5</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
